\paragraph{Features learned by FB.}
\Cref{fig:fb-features} shows the features of a trained FB critic with two features, where they can be drawn in the plane.
FB gives the rewarded state A ($3$) exactly the same features as the unrewarded state B ($4$), to numerical precision in all ten runs.
The average feature vector of the future after $a_+$ therefore equals that after $a_-$, which is the condition of \cref{lem:bottleneck-loss}, and FB predicts the same future and the same value ($2.14$) for both actions.

